  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Entry and ownership",
      "items": [
        "main starts application.New. Application validates configuration, owns Redis and composes :8080 HTTP. Startup: 10s. Shutdown: 30s. Sources: main.go:15\u201359; internal/application/application.go:117\u2013174.",
        "/chat and /chat/stream share completion policy. /usage and /limits use the same admission gates; /health and /models are public. Sources: internal/handler/chat.go:32\u201343; internal/handler/limits.go:17\u201343."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Routing, retrieval and cache",
      "items": [
        "Route the original question before retrieval. Over 500 bytes or a complexity keyword selects the powerful tier. RAG filters project and active state before ranking; up to four chunks at similarity \u22650.80. Sources: internal/router/router.go:41\u201360; internal/rag/rag.go:22\u201331,116\u2013158.",
        "RAG misses/errors continue ungrounded. Cache errors become misses. Cache similarity \u22650.95; default TTL 24h. A hit skips chat generation and usage increments but still requires embedding calls. Sources: internal/completion/completion.go:129\u2013210; internal/cache/semantic.go:18\u201324,112\u2013222.",
        "Cache scope: project hash, primary routed model, schema, corpus revision and prompt-policy-v1. Fallback answers retain the original routed namespace. Sources: internal/cache/namespace.go:22\u201335; internal/completion/completion.go:157\u2013159,213\u2013242."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Prompt boundaries",
      "items": [
        "One fixed system policy. Optional JSON-encoded untrusted references in a user message. Original question in a separate user message. Input cannot create API roles or enter trusted policy. Source: internal/completion/input.go:5\u201343.",
        "Same builder for JSON, SSE and fallback. No tools, classifier, phrase blocklist or output screening. Tests prove serialization and wiring; model-level resistance is unmeasured. Sources: internal/provider/openai.go:64\u201392; internal/completion/completion.go:213\u2013216; internal/completion/stream.go:80\u201389."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Fallback and settlement",
      "items": [
        "Try one distinct configured fallback on transport error or HTTP 408/429/5xx before output. Cancellation/deadline errors do not retry. Defaults equal primary, so default routes do not retry. Sources: internal/application/application.go:94\u2013108; internal/completion/completion.go:213\u2013255; internal/completion/stream.go:80\u2013100.",
        "Settle once at exhaustion or Close. Without provider usage, estimate policy, references, question and received output. Mark estimates; settlement outlives cancellation with a 5s budget. Cache only complete nonempty streams. Sources: internal/completion/input.go:46\u201351; internal/completion/stream.go:154\u2013240."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "State and operator paths",
      "items": [
        "Redis boxes are logical groups in one configured Redis Stack instance. No persistent volume is declared in Compose. Key quotas use HMAC key ID; concurrency/RAG/cache/usage use project identity. Sources: internal/application/application.go:124\u2013161; docker-compose.yml:1\u201326; internal/middleware/ratelimit.go:15\u201329.",
        "project-key provisions fingerprints. rag-import reads reviewed text; rag.Upload embeds and atomically replaces chunks while advancing corpus revision. Sources: cmd/project-key/main.go:18\u201345; cmd/rag-import/main.go:16\u201345; internal/rag/rag.go:55\u2013113.",
        "cache-eval measures classification with real embeddings; provider-smoke checks a running gateway. Reports are opt-in, outside serving/normal CI. CI builds, vets, checks format/race tests, and rejects skipped Redis-backed tests. Sources: cmd/cache-eval/main.go:36\u201395; cmd/provider-smoke/main.go:56\u2013131; .github/workflows/ci.yml:8\u201372."
      ]
    }
  ]
